{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I have the full picture of task7. The task file confirms the test method exactly matches the prompt. Let me now check the key details needed to write an accurate test:\n\n1. The current state: handler doesn't have HumanLoop/Ctrl/Dream/Learning functions yet → the test should detect this (RED phase).\n\n2. The boundary test:\n   - `human-loop --dry-run '测试主题'` → output contains `sense_loop`. Let me check what `BuildHumanLoop` produces currently (in cmd/human_loop.go it calls `pb.BuildHumanLoop(topic, map)` and prints content). The output should contain `sense_loop` based on the SENSE methodology.\n   - `dream --dry-run` → only lists completed & not-dreamed jobs. Need to check current `selectPendingJobs` behavior and what the output format is. Currently `runDreamDryRun` prints `[DRY-RUN] Pending jobs (%d): %v`.\n   - `ctrl` (no --job) → reports `--job flag is required` exit non-zero.\n\n3. Exception:\n   - `learning job_N` (doing/tasks.json not exists) → reports `tasks.json not found` exit non-zero no panic.\n   - `ctrl --dry-run --job job_N` (doing dir not exists) → reports `doing directory not found` exit non-zero.\n\nWait, let me re-read the exception part carefully. The prompt says:\n\n\"异常（learning 缺数据 + ctrl doing 目录不存在）：前置条件 = build 成功；输入 = `learning job_N`（doing/tasks.json 不存在）、`ctrl --dry-run --job job_N`（doing 目录不存在）；操作 = 运行；预期 = learning 报 `tasks.json not found` exit 非 0 不 panic；ctrl 报 `doing directory not found` exit 非 0。\"\n\nHmm, but the current ctrl code (runCtrlDryRun) does NOT check for \"doing directory not found\" — it just calls `SaveCtrlPrompt(jID, rickDir)`. So this \"doing directory not found\" is a NEW behavior that task7 will implement (the handler.CtrlDryRun needs to check doing directory existence).\n\nActually wait, let me think about this more carefully. The task7 spec says ctrl should be migrated to handler.Ctrl / handler.CtrlDryRun. And the test method expects ctrl --dry-run --job job_N (where doing dir doesn't exist) to report \"doing directory not found\".\n\nCurrently the ctrl dry-run doesn't do this check. So this is a new assertion that task7 must implement.\n\nLet me check the builder's BuildCtrl / GenerateCtrlPromptFile / SaveCtrlPrompt to understand what \"doing directory not found\" behavior would be. Actually, since task7 hasn't been implemented yet, the current behavior is:\n- ctrl --dry-run --job job_N → SaveCtrlPrompt generates a prompt (regardless of whether doing dir exists).\n\nSo the test asserting \"doing directory not found\" would FAIL currently (RED), which is correct for TDD.\n\nBut wait — I need to be careful. The test method says ctrl reports \"doing directory not found\". But does the spec (task7.md key results) mention this? Let me check. The key results don't explicitly mention \"doing directory not found\" for ctrl. But the test method (which is the authoritative acceptance criteria) says:\n\n\"ctrl 报 `doing directory not found` exit 非 0\"\n\nSo the test script must check this. However, I need to think: is this check about the ctrl command's new behavior in the handler? The task7 handler.Ctrl/CtrlDryRun will presumably validate that the job's doing directory exists before generating the ctrl prompt.\n\nActually, let me look more carefully. The task7.md says for ctrl: \"cli 保留 NewCtrlCmd（--job 必传校验 + 调 handler）；迁出 runCtrl/runCtrlDryRun → handler.Ctrl/handler.CtrlDryRun\". And for the ctrl.md template, \"注入路径而非内容（去掉 tasks_json_content 快照，pi 自行 read）\". So the ctrl prompt now injects paths (job_id/doing_dir/plan_dir/tasks_json path). To inject doing_dir path, the handler would need to resolve the doing dir. If it doesn't exist, \"doing directory not found\" makes sense as a new validation.\n\nOK so my test script needs to:\n1. Build (normal path) + go test.\n2. Boundary:\n   - human-loop --dry-run '测试主题' → contains 'sense_loop'\n   - dream --dry-run → only lists completed & not-dreamed jobs (need fixture setup)\n   - ctrl (no --job) → '--job flag is required' + non-zero exit\n3. Exception:\n   - learning job_N (no doing/tasks.json) → 'tasks.json not found' + non-zero, no panic\n   - ctrl --dry-run --job job_N (no doing dir) → 'doing directory not found' + non-zero\n\nLet me check the builder's functions to understand what `BuildHumanLoop`, `SaveCtrlPrompt`, `BuildDream` etc. currently produce, to know:\n- Whether human-loop dry-run output contains 'sense_loop' (it should, since the template uses SENSE methodology).\n- What dream dry-run output looks like (format for \"Pending jobs\").\n\nLet me check the builder."}}
