"本 task 改写 ctrl.md 为 pi JSONL 语义\"). So yes, it's fair game.\n\nBut let me make the check lenient enough: check that the old \"type = ...\" NDJSON description is gone AND a pi JSONL term is present. I'll use a single assertion combining both (must not have old markers, must have new marker).\n\nActually, I'll split into two separate error messages for clarity:\n- If old Claude NDJSON markers still present → error.\n- If no pi JSONL markers → error.\n\nNow let me also think about the \"act-path.md 引用改 runtime trace 占位\" part. The current ctrl.md references `act-path.md` (multiple times) and `raw_session_coding.log`. Task7 should change act-path references to runtime trace (trace.md). But the prompt says \"act-path.md 引用改为 runtime trace（task8 一并）\" — wait, let me re-read.\n\nFrom the prompt 逐命令改动明细 for ctrl: \"ctrl.md 模板 stale（重要）：当前描述 claude code 的 NDJSON 格式...——本 task 改写 ctrl.md 为 pi JSONL 语义；act-path.md 引用改为 runtime trace（task8 一并）\"\n\nSo the \"act-path.md 引用改 runtime trace\" is deferred to task8 (\"task8 一并\"). Only the NDJSON→JSONL rewrite is task7. So I should NOT check for act-path.md removal (that's task8). I should only check for the NDJSON→JSONL rewrite.\n\nActually wait, let me re-read key result 3: \"ctrl.md 模板改写为 pi JSONL 语义（去 claude code NDJSON 描述），act-path 引用改 runtime trace 占位\". Hmm, key result 3 says act-path reference → runtime trace placeholder is part of this task. But the 逐命令改动明细 says \"task8 一并\".\n\nThere's a slight contradiction. Let me be conservative: only check the NDJSON→JSONL rewrite (which is unambiguously task7), NOT the act-path removal (which is ambiguous/deferred). The NDJSON→JSONL check is: remove `type = \"system\"/\"assistant\"/\"user\"/\"result\"` and add pi JSONL markers.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The key result 3 clearly states both. But the 逐命令改动明细 says act-path → task8. Given the ambiguity, I'll only assert the NDJSON→JSONL part, which is unambiguous and core. I'll skip the act-path check.\n\nNow let me finalize the tes