k 迁编排\". Does \"迁编排\" mean the scan functions move in task7, or just the orchestration (Dream/DreamDryRun) moves while scan functions stay for now?\n\nLet me re-read key result 4 very carefully:\n\"4. dream 的 4 个扫描函数（selectPendingJobs/getDreamProcessedJobs/discoverCompletedJobs/jobNumber）迁 workspace（本 task 迁编排，tasks.json 极薄读取器类型定义在 task8 落地）\"\n\nAnd the 逐命令改动明细 dream section:\n\"迁出 dreamWorkflow→handler.Dream、runDreamDryRun→handler.DreamDryRun、selectPendingJobs/getDreamProcessedJobs/discoverCompletedJobs/jobNumber（4 个确定性扫描过滤函数）\"\n\"扫描过滤留在 Go（确定性输入过滤，决定哪些 job 要 dream）：discoverCompletedJobs 依赖的 executor.LoadTasksJSON + TasksJSON.GetAllTasks() + TaskState.Status 迁 workspace（极薄读取器，task8 显式落地）\"\n\nSo the 4 scan functions migrate OUT of cmd (迁出) — to workspace. The \"极薄读取器\" (thin reader) is what lands in task8, meaning in task7 the scan functions use executor.LoadTasksJSON (still). So in task7, workspace gets the 4 scan functions (still using executor for now).\n\nSo checking that workspace has these 4 functions is valid for task7. I'll include it.\n\nBut wait, there's still a subtle risk: `discoverCompletedJobs` uses `executor.LoadTasksJSON` in task7, so workspace will import executor in task7 (until task8 swaps to thin reader). That's fine — I'm only checking function presence in workspace, not imports.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider whether the functions move to `workspace` or somewhere else. The key result says \"迁 workspace\". So `internal/workspace`. I'll check `internal/workspace/*.go` for these 4 function definitions.\n\nOK let me finalize. I'll write comprehensive but carefully-scoped checks.\n\nLet me also decide: should the 4 scan functions check be strict (all 4 required) or lenient (any subset)? I'll make it: report missing functions individually (collect into one error message listing which are missing). This way it's informative.\n\nNow let me write the actual script.\n\nLet me think about the JSON structure of tasks.json for the fixture. I'll 